  (text "ONE POWER SOURCE IN REV A: USB-C PD ONLY — no barrel jack, no PoE.\n  USB-C: VBUS -> F101 (PTC) -> VCC_5V   — direct, no OR-ing diode.\nPD negotiates 5V at the connector, so there is no wide-Vin buck and no\nintermediate rail. VCC_5V feeds the ADM3053 and U103 (5V -> 3V3 for the S3,\nW5500 and ADM3053 VIO).\n\nNO OR-ing DIODES (H19a). With a single source there is nothing to OR, and a\nSchottky would cost ~0.35V — leaving the ADM3053 only ~150mV above its 4.5V\nminimum and sagging isoPower. D103 AND D104 ARE NOT FITTED. Rev B reinstates\nOR-ing with an ideal-diode controller rather than a Schottky, to avoid that\nsame drop.\nNote this makes the CFG1 hazard below MORE direct, not less: with no series\ndiode, a 20V PD request lands on VCC_5V through F101 alone.\n\nPoE is deferred to rev B by decision (H19) — see the PoE note on this sheet.\n\nUSB-PD SINK: U104 = CH224K, real PD negotiation on CC1/CC2.\n\n*** SAFETY-CRITICAL: CFG1 IS HARD-TIED TO PD_VDD. DO NOT CUT THIS. ***\nCH224K selects the requested voltage by CFG1/2/3 level: CFG1 high = 5V.\nThe datasheet warns that if CFG1 is FLOATING at power-up the chip requests 20V.\nThis board cannot survive that: 20V would pass D103 onto VCC_5V and destroy the\nADM3053 (VCC abs max ~6V) and U103's input. CFG1 is therefore wired straight to\nPD_VDD in copper — NOT to an MCU GPIO. The MCU is powered FROM this rail, so it\ncannot possibly configure the PD chip before the rail it depends on exists.\nCFG2/CFG3 have internal pulldowns and are don't-care when CFG1 is high.\n\nCH224K DP/DM are deliberately NOT connected to USB_DP/USB_DM. Those pins are for\nlegacy BC1.2/QC negotiation; wiring them to the data pair would corrupt the USB\nlink we need for NCM/R60/programming. PD runs entirely over CC.\n\nThe 5.1k CC pulldowns are GONE — the CH224K drives CC itself. Leaving fixed Rd\nresistors in parallel would present the wrong impedance and break PD signalling.\n\nPD_PG (open-drain, active low) is brought out to the MCU as a power-good input.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE FAB: R106 (VBUS->VDD series, 1k) and R107 (VBUS sense series, 100k).\nThe datasheet requires a series resistor on each but does not state the values in\nthe text; these are plausible, not confirmed. Check against WCH's reference design."
    (at 40 175 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "3c39814c-e46c-414b-9ce8-5aa368cd2fbe"))

  (text "POE IS DEFERRED TO REV B — BY DECISION (H19, 2026-07-25), NOT BY A TOOLING FAULT.\n\nRev A is USB-C PD only. The Ag97005-FL module was this board's risk\nconcentration: 56 x 14 mm on a board meant to be as small as practical, NOT on\nLCSC so JLCPCB cannot assemble it, hand-soldered, and its land pattern is not\nfab-confident. USB-C PD already negotiates 5V / 3W, which powers everything —\nso rev A proves the whole protocol and firmware stack with no unconfirmed\nfootprints and no hand-fit parts. That is the actual point of the project.\n\nNOT FITTED IN REV A: U101 (Ag97005-FL), R105 (class programming), D103/D104\n(OR-ing diodes) and the 57V isolation zone. U101 has no footprint in\ndbcanary.kicad_pcb — this sheet and the board agree.\n\nREV B TAP POINTS — already brought out, on the Ethernet sheet:\n   ETH_CT_TD     T401 TD centre tap     mode A (phantom, on the data pairs)\n   ETH_CT_RD     T401 RD centre tap     mode A\n   ETH_SPARE_1   J401 pins 4/5          mode B (spare pairs)\n   ETH_SPARE_2   J401 pins 7/8          mode B\nThese were POE_MODEA/B_* until H19c renamed them: a POE_* net on a board with\nno PoE misleads a reviewer. In rev A the spare pairs are Bob Smith terminated\n(R404/R405, 75R, into BOB_SMITH) so all four pairs are properly terminated\nrather than left dangling; rev B taps them for mode B instead. Because the taps\nalready exist, rev B is a power-section change and not a redesign.\n\nERC IS CLEAN: zero errors. The six former power_pin_not_driven errors were\nresolved with PWR_FLAG — correctly, not silenced. Rev A's rails genuinely ARE\ndriven, from J102's VBUS pin, which is a passive connector pin: precisely the\ncase PWR_FLAG exists for. Flags sit on VCC_5V, VCC_3V3, GND, VISO, CAN_GND and\nPD_VDD (the last derived through R106, a passive resistor)."
    (at 40 148 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "71bd0d32-31f7-411d-a3b8-89dd3b752089"))

